          {
            "kind": "styled",
            "id": "b210",
            "text": "Postmortem: DNS resolution errors on March 4, 2026",
            "style": {
              "size": 28,
              "weight": "bold"
            }
          },
          {
            "kind": "styled",
            "id": "b211",
            "text": "Hannah Okafor · 2026-03-06",
            "style": {
              "size": 13,
              "color": "#5f6b7a"
            }
          },
          {
            "kind": "divider",
            "id": "b212"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "b213",
            "text": "For 23 minutes on March 4, between 14:11 and 14:34 UTC, some authoritative DNS queries for zones on Cloudflare returned SERVFAIL. About 4 percent of queries in that window were affected, concentrated in two European locations."
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "b214",
            "text": "Root cause: a configuration push that changed the zone database sharding rolled out to two data centers whose local cache still held the previous shard map. Queries that hashed to a moved shard could not find their zone. The rollout was automatically halted when error rates crossed the threshold, and the two locations were drained while the caches refreshed."
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "b215",
            "text": "What we changed: a shard map change now invalidates the local cache in the same transaction, and the canary stage of the rollout waits for a full cache refresh before proceeding. We are sorry for the disruption; the Status page carries the full timeline."
          },
